WEBVTT

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:08.908
Come on. Santa Anna didn't care
about the rules of war.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:11.775
If he had executed
Davy Crockett at the Alamo

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.802
he would have considered it
a point of pride.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.712
All right, put it this way...

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.547
in 1836, Davy Crockett
was what, 49?

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.382
Quite old
for the standards of the time.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.820
His days as an Indian fighter
were well behind him.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.949
He was just an ex-Congressman...
all reputation.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.083
Now, this is not a man

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.594
who was about to fight
till his last breath, Miles.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.528
The situation was hopeless.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.996
He was out of ammunition.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.796
The Mexican army was storming
the Alamo's battlements.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.200
He would have surrendered.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.398
It's as logical as that...
simple.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.907
I'm not saying
it couldn't have happened.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.636
I'm just saying
there's no proof.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.303
You are both wrong.

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.438
The only real question
is whether you believe

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.448
in the legend
of Davy Crockett or not.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.972
If you do, then there should be

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.713
no doubt in your mind
that he died a hero's death.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.744
If you do not believe
in the legend

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.689
then he was just a man

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.783
and it does not matter
how he died.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.926
Well, I guess
that settles that.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.026
I guess so.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.132
Enter.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:18.636
Kor...

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:19.872
Nuq'nuh, Worf.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.642
It's good to see you,
my friend.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.647
I welcome you to my home.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:27.711
May I offer you
some refreshment?

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.981
I would be honored to share
a bottle of bloodwine

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.516
with the son of Mogh.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.761
I heard the news about Jadzia.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.970
She died a warrior.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.273
I expected nothing less.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.222
To absent comrades.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.786
Mmm! 2309.
Very good.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.956
Sit.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.431
Oh.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:16.799
The war goes, um,
well for you, Worf?

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:20.533
Um, a long list of victories
to your credit, I trust?

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.804
I have been... fortunate.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:27.108
Oh-ho-ho, the way of the warrior
is not a humble path.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.445
Show some pride
in your accomplishments.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.710
You've earned it.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.877
I will try.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.050
And does the war go well
for you, Kor?

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:44.153
No, Worf,
it does not go well for me.

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:48.326
It seems my... services

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.768
are not required
in the present conflict.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:54.637
But you are Kor...
a Dahar Master

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:58.007
the man who held the Korma Pass
against T'nag.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:01.945
Your reputation alone should
have assured you a command.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:06.179
I also have a reputation
for a certain ruthless quality

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.949
towards those who
would stand in my way.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.388
Mind you,
it's not entirely undeserved.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:14.951
In truth, I rather enjoy being
feared by my fellow officers.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:19.464
However, there's a price
to be paid for such...

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:22.434
single-minded devotion
to one's ambition.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:25.096
I've made enemies...
perhaps

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.231
more than were necessary.

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:33.978
I have no influence left
in the Empire.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:37.312
Even as our entire race
grapples with the Dominion

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.581
there's no place
for an old man

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:45.216
with too many enemies
and not enough friends.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:51.461
That's why
I've come here tonight.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.658
It's not easy

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.693
for me to beg you for help...

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:00.865
but I have nowhere else to turn.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:06.210
Help me fight again, Worf.

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:11.047
Help me end my life
as I've lived it...

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.177
as a warrior.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:22.686
How many more reports
does the High Council require?

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:25.061
As many as last time.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.896
And Starfleet is still
waiting for your signature

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.526
on these repair requests.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:34.138
There will come a day, Darok

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:38.269
when your services as my aide
will no longer be required.

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:42.771
I look forward to that day
with great anticipation.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:43.782
Until then...

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:46.977
Ah, Worf!

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.247
Good to see you.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.483
Thank you, Darok.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:05:00.992
It's a pity Captain Sisko
frowns on summary executions.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.229
What can I do for you?

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:07.296
Kor, the Dahar Master
came to see me last night.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.205
He has been unable
to find a command and I...

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.368
Tell me you're not going

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.139
to ask me
to give that man a ship.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.146
Well, I had hoped...

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.375
Then your hopes are in vain.

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:19.283
That man is not welcome
in my House

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:20.752
and I will certainly
not have him

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:22.277
commanding a ship in my fleet.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:25.291
General, Kor is a friend,
and I have already...

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.292
Not another word!

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.317
Do you hear?
Not one word!

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:35.899
Now get out of here
before I forget we are brothers.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:52.330
I plan to attack
the Trelka V Starbase

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:54.896
then push deeper
into Cardassian territory.

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:57.204
I'll hit the Manora shipyards

00:07:57.242 --> 00:08:00.609
the Jem'Hadar breeding
facility on Sheva II

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:03.615
the supply depots
in the Borias Cluster.

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:05.082
It would take half
the Ninth Fleet

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:06.914
just to destroy Trelka V.

00:08:06.985 --> 00:08:10.580
I don't intend to destroy
the base, just damage it...

00:08:10.622 --> 00:08:12.180
throw them off-balance

00:08:12.224 --> 00:08:15.455
then move on
to the next target.

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:18.930
Imagine... the chaos we'll cause

00:08:18.964 --> 00:08:21.398
once we're in
behind their lines.

00:08:21.433 --> 00:08:22.798
A cavalry raid.

00:08:23.902 --> 00:08:26.530
Ancient Earth soldiers
mounted on horseback.

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.802
They had the speed
to charge behind enemy lines

00:08:28.841 --> 00:08:29.933
to stir up trouble

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:32.500
and the mobility
to keep from being caught.

00:08:32.544 --> 00:08:35.035
How many ships will you take?

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.877
Five birds-of-prey.

00:08:36.915 --> 00:08:38.610
Battle cruisers are too slow

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:40.413
too unwieldy
for a mission like this.

00:08:40.452 --> 00:08:42.920
Do you want to take the Defiant?

00:08:42.955 --> 00:08:45.549
Perhaps the Defiant
should remain here

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:51.291
just in case the Jem'Hadar try
their own "cavalry raid," hmm?

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:54.128
But it may be prudent
for the Defiant

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:56.532
and a dozen or so
other starships

00:08:56.568 --> 00:08:58.536
to be waiting for us
when we return.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.539
You mean you might be bringing
company back with you?

00:09:01.573 --> 00:09:04.701
I'm sure you'll be
ready to welcome them.

00:09:04.743 --> 00:09:06.608
With phasers charged.

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:19.121
Our disruptor targeting sensors
need to be replaced

00:09:19.157 --> 00:09:21.125
as well as our
guidance system relays.

00:09:21.159 --> 00:09:23.593
Make a note of that
for Chief O'Brien.

00:09:23.629 --> 00:09:25.859
He should give the Ch'Tang
first priority.

00:09:27.032 --> 00:09:29.432
So, if you have something
to ask me, do it now

00:09:29.468 --> 00:09:31.629
before Darok buries me
under more paperwork.

00:09:33.438 --> 00:09:35.303
I wish to speak
with you about Kor.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.830
Now, I know you have
strong feelings about...

00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:39.139
Clear the Bridge!

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:55.149
I did not expect
to hear anything

00:09:55.193 --> 00:09:57.423
further on this
subject from you.

00:09:57.462 --> 00:09:59.726
And I did not expect
to be forbidden

00:09:59.765 --> 00:10:01.790
to speak with you
on any subject.

00:10:01.833 --> 00:10:04.165
Have I become a shuVak

00:10:04.202 --> 00:10:07.467
to be ordered about
like Darok?

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:10.909
No.

00:10:10.943 --> 00:10:12.968
Of course not.

00:10:13.011 --> 00:10:15.479
Very well.

00:10:15.514 --> 00:10:18.506
Talk and be done with it.

00:10:21.286 --> 00:10:26.952
Kor came to see me,
asking my help as a friend.

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.254
He is an old man

00:10:31.296 --> 00:10:34.322
with no family and no influence
left in the Empire.

00:10:34.366 --> 00:10:37.858
He asked nothing
except for the chance

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:40.133
to fight and die
as a Klingon warrior.

00:10:40.172 --> 00:10:42.140
I told him I would
speak with you

00:10:42.174 --> 00:10:44.574
about finding him
a command in the fleet.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:50.242
I would not give that man
the gnawed bones of my last meal

00:10:50.282 --> 00:10:53.012
much less command of a ship.

00:10:53.051 --> 00:10:54.348
But why?

00:10:54.386 --> 00:10:56.911
There is no blood feud
between our Houses

00:10:56.955 --> 00:10:59.219
and Kor has said
he has not even met you.

00:11:02.127 --> 00:11:07.224
You can wound a man
without ever seeing his face.

00:11:11.269 --> 00:11:14.500
When I was a boy,
my family still lived

00:11:14.539 --> 00:11:15.972
in the lowlands
of Ketha Province.

00:11:16.074 --> 00:11:18.668
We had very little,
but it didn't matter.

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:21.338
We were a family of warriors.

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:24.076
15 generations had served
as soldiers of the Empire

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:28.416
but my father had
higher hopes for me.

00:11:28.453 --> 00:11:32.321
He wanted his son
to become an officer.

00:11:32.357 --> 00:11:34.825
It took a great deal of effort

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:39.092
but eventually, he found someone
willing to sponsor me.

00:11:39.131 --> 00:11:42.897
I passed my entrance exam
on my first attempt

00:11:42.934 --> 00:11:45.300
and all that remained
was final approval

00:11:45.337 --> 00:11:48.738
by the Oversight Council...
a simple formality.

00:11:50.242 --> 00:11:52.904
My application was rejected

00:11:52.944 --> 00:11:58.405
by one member
of that council... Kor.

00:11:59.718 --> 00:12:01.310
Why?

00:12:01.353 --> 00:12:04.550
"Why?"

00:12:04.589 --> 00:12:08.047
Kor's family descends
from the lmperial Court itself.

00:12:08.093 --> 00:12:09.321
Kor is "of the blood"...

00:12:09.361 --> 00:12:12.387
born to rule
by the divine will of Kahless

00:12:12.431 --> 00:12:13.693
and what was I?

00:12:13.732 --> 00:12:16.792
A boy from the Ketha lowlands.

00:12:16.835 --> 00:12:18.393
He could not bear the thought

00:12:18.437 --> 00:12:22.430
of someone like me joining
the elite officer ranks

00:12:22.474 --> 00:12:24.942
and so, to my father's
embarrassment

00:12:24.976 --> 00:12:26.910
and my everlasting shame...

00:12:26.945 --> 00:12:30.381
my application was denied.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.242
And with the mark
of Kor on my record

00:12:33.285 --> 00:12:36.254
I could not join
even as a common soldier.

00:12:36.288 --> 00:12:39.985
I spent five years
as a civilian laborer

00:12:40.025 --> 00:12:41.959
aboard General
ShiVang's flagship.

00:12:41.993 --> 00:12:47.158
Then... as fortune
would have it

00:12:47.199 --> 00:12:52.000
the Romulans made a foolhardy
attempt to board our ship.

00:12:52.104 --> 00:12:56.268
I earned
a battlefield commission.

00:12:56.308 --> 00:12:59.505
Unfortunately...

00:12:59.544 --> 00:13:04.243
my father did not live
to see that glorious day.

00:13:09.788 --> 00:13:12.052
And if Kor had had his way

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:15.856
I would still be
a civilian on that ship

00:13:15.894 --> 00:13:17.725
cleaning the officers' mess.

00:13:17.763 --> 00:13:19.526
I understand

00:13:19.564 --> 00:13:22.624
but I must tell you
that using my own authority

00:13:22.667 --> 00:13:25.465
I appointed Kor
an officer in the Ninth Fleet.

00:13:27.005 --> 00:13:30.907
Made him an officer...
just like that.

00:13:30.942 --> 00:13:34.309
That's the difference
between his name and mine...

00:13:34.346 --> 00:13:38.646
his opens doors,
mine closes them.

00:13:38.683 --> 00:13:40.082
I did not anticipate...

00:13:40.118 --> 00:13:41.085
It's done!

00:13:41.119 --> 00:13:43.679
Your apology is not sought

00:13:43.722 --> 00:13:45.986
but know this, Worf...

00:13:46.057 --> 00:13:49.993
Kor is your responsibility.

00:13:50.028 --> 00:13:53.020
I want nothing
to do with him.

00:13:58.737 --> 00:14:00.261
Do you...
do you remember

00:14:00.305 --> 00:14:02.899
breaking into
the Duke's harem on Renavi?

00:14:02.941 --> 00:14:05.102
Oh.

00:14:05.143 --> 00:14:07.270
How could I forget that?

00:14:07.312 --> 00:14:09.872
That is one of Curzon's
favorite memories.

00:14:12.117 --> 00:14:14.051
Hi.

00:14:16.054 --> 00:14:16.952
Hello.

00:14:17.055 --> 00:14:19.319
Come and join us, my friend.

00:14:19.357 --> 00:14:22.520
Uh... I am on duty.

00:14:22.561 --> 00:14:25.052
I'll see you later.

00:14:25.096 --> 00:14:26.085
Mmm.

00:14:27.866 --> 00:14:30.130
It's good to see you again, Kor.

00:14:30.168 --> 00:14:31.601
Mm-hmm.

00:14:33.605 --> 00:14:36.631
Still the same old Dax...

00:14:36.675 --> 00:14:38.336
and yet not.

00:14:38.376 --> 00:14:40.606
General Martok will not
give you a command.

00:14:40.645 --> 00:14:43.478
Uh... kesh!

00:14:43.515 --> 00:14:44.812
He says that

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:46.977
you struck his name
from an officers list

00:14:47.085 --> 00:14:50.077
because his family comes
from the Ketha lowlands.

00:14:50.121 --> 00:14:51.611
Did I?

00:14:53.058 --> 00:14:54.958
I don't recall.

00:14:54.993 --> 00:14:58.394
Of course, there were
so many officer lists.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.091
I suppose it's possible.

00:15:00.131 --> 00:15:03.931
It is an unworthy reason to bar
a man from serving the Empire.

00:15:05.737 --> 00:15:07.034
Worf, you've been living

00:15:07.072 --> 00:15:10.872
among this democratic rabble
for too long.

00:15:10.909 --> 00:15:12.342
I know your bloodline.

00:15:12.377 --> 00:15:15.744
We both come from noble Houses.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:19.147
Among our people,
that still counts for something.

00:15:19.184 --> 00:15:21.948
If Martok is a true Klingon,
he should appreciate that.

00:15:22.053 --> 00:15:23.077
He does not.

00:15:26.758 --> 00:15:29.488
Did he revoke my commission?

00:15:29.527 --> 00:15:31.825
No. You will serve
aboard the Ch'Tang...

00:15:33.164 --> 00:15:34.688
as Third Officer.

00:15:34.733 --> 00:15:36.826
Third?!

00:15:40.438 --> 00:15:42.565
Oh, well... huh, no matter.

00:15:42.607 --> 00:15:45.974
I've overcome greater obstacles.

00:15:46.011 --> 00:15:48.809
Thank you, Worf.
You're a true friend.

00:15:49.814 --> 00:15:52.715
You will report aboard at 0700

00:15:52.751 --> 00:15:55.948
and stay out of Martok's way.

00:15:55.987 --> 00:15:59.514
He will not even know
I am there.

00:16:02.694 --> 00:16:03.922
Worf!

00:16:04.029 --> 00:16:06.554
Uh... what was the
name of that ship?

00:16:06.598 --> 00:16:08.156
Oh, the Ch'Tang.

00:16:08.199 --> 00:16:10.064
Ch'Tang! Of course.

00:16:10.101 --> 00:16:11.466
I'll see you there.

00:16:26.117 --> 00:16:27.448
All decks report ready.

00:16:27.485 --> 00:16:28.543
Defense systems on-line.

00:16:28.586 --> 00:16:29.712
Engine room standing by.

00:16:29.754 --> 00:16:31.483
Transporter room reports
that our last crew members

00:16:31.523 --> 00:16:32.490
have beamed aboard.

00:16:32.524 --> 00:16:33.491
Very well.

00:16:33.525 --> 00:16:34.492
Signal the squadron.

00:16:34.526 --> 00:16:35.959
Prepare to get under way.

00:16:35.994 --> 00:16:37.484
Stand by to cloak.

00:16:37.529 --> 00:16:38.518
Aye, sir.

00:16:38.563 --> 00:16:43.364
Helm, set course 325 mark 003.

00:16:43.401 --> 00:16:45.198
Full impulse till we
clear the outer marker.

00:16:45.236 --> 00:16:46.965
Then go to...

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:52.667
Third Officer Kor
reporting for duty.

00:16:52.711 --> 00:16:54.269
The Dahar Master.

00:16:56.614 --> 00:16:58.741
Take your station.

00:17:10.928 --> 00:17:13.089
Return to your duties

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:15.360
or I will find a crew that can.

00:17:15.399 --> 00:17:18.857
Helmsman, I gave you
an order.

00:17:18.903 --> 00:17:20.461
ChaH-Veh!

00:17:29.513 --> 00:17:31.413
Kor...

00:17:31.448 --> 00:17:34.417
here on our ship.

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:38.918
Don't you have
something to do?

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.548
No.

00:17:41.592 --> 00:17:43.651
Then find something!

00:17:52.403 --> 00:17:54.803
It's an honor to have you
aboard with us.

00:17:54.839 --> 00:17:57.501
Ah, thank you very much.

00:17:57.541 --> 00:17:59.736
Welcome, Dahar Master.

00:18:11.088 --> 00:18:13.022
So what did Kor say
when he met you?

00:18:13.057 --> 00:18:15.389
The usual.

00:18:15.426 --> 00:18:18.918
I have the same conversation
over and over again.

00:18:18.963 --> 00:18:20.828
Everyone's shocked at first.

00:18:20.865 --> 00:18:22.833
Then they start
scanning my face

00:18:22.867 --> 00:18:25.768
for signs of the person
they knew as Dax.

00:18:25.803 --> 00:18:27.498
"It can't be.

00:18:27.538 --> 00:18:29.438
"Is it really you?

00:18:29.473 --> 00:18:32.340
"Oh, I do see
a little Jadzia in the eyes

00:18:32.376 --> 00:18:34.776
a little Curzon in the smile."

00:18:34.812 --> 00:18:36.939
Isn't there a period
of adjustment

00:18:37.014 --> 00:18:38.948
that joined Trills
have to go through

00:18:39.016 --> 00:18:40.574
where people
are comparing them

00:18:40.618 --> 00:18:41.585
to previous hosts?

00:18:41.619 --> 00:18:43.814
I'm, I'm sure it'll pass.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:47.721
You're right.

00:18:47.758 --> 00:18:49.953
The last five Dax hosts
went through this.

00:18:50.027 --> 00:18:51.016
Ah.

00:18:53.163 --> 00:18:54.687
That wasn't bad.

00:18:54.732 --> 00:18:56.529
You'd make
a pretty good Counselor.

00:18:56.567 --> 00:18:57.795
You want to trade jobs?

00:18:57.835 --> 00:19:00.429
Oh, yeah... people would love
bringing their problems to me.

00:19:00.471 --> 00:19:01.904
"You dreamt about what?

00:19:01.939 --> 00:19:02.906
"You're crazy.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:04.464
"Now get out of my office.

00:19:04.508 --> 00:19:06.169
Next patient."

00:19:07.778 --> 00:19:09.905
It's funny you should
mention dreams.

00:19:10.014 --> 00:19:12.915
Ever since
my conversation with Kor

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:15.578
I have had the most
intense dreams about him.

00:19:15.619 --> 00:19:16.779
Like what?

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.913
Being on a Klingon
Bridge together...

00:19:19.023 --> 00:19:20.513
going off into battle...

00:19:20.557 --> 00:19:22.081
drinking bloodwine...

00:19:22.126 --> 00:19:23.684
which still makes me gag

00:19:23.727 --> 00:19:25.024
by the way.

00:19:25.062 --> 00:19:26.723
Singing songs...

00:19:26.764 --> 00:19:29.665
A part of me wants to be
out there with him now.

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:31.600
I hope he's all right.

00:19:31.635 --> 00:19:33.660
I mean, I know I'm sort
of contradicting

00:19:33.704 --> 00:19:35.228
what I just said
about wanting

00:19:35.272 --> 00:19:37.502
to set myself apart
from my previous hosts

00:19:37.541 --> 00:19:41.204
but the memories I have
of being with him

00:19:41.245 --> 00:19:42.303
are so vivid.

00:19:42.346 --> 00:19:44.280
I can't bear the
thought of losing him.

00:19:44.315 --> 00:19:47.182
I'd give almost anything
for the chance to...

00:19:47.217 --> 00:19:49.651
be together just one more time...

00:19:49.687 --> 00:19:53.214
the two of us side by side,
just like it used to be.

00:19:57.528 --> 00:19:59.120
Do you need something?

00:20:01.298 --> 00:20:02.458
No.

00:20:04.935 --> 00:20:06.562
Nothing.

00:20:11.608 --> 00:20:15.169
So, what's your
professional opinion?

00:20:15.212 --> 00:20:17.806
Mmm... you're crazy.

00:20:17.848 --> 00:20:19.907
Next patient.

00:20:24.955 --> 00:20:26.616
What's the matter with you?

00:20:26.657 --> 00:20:28.557
Someone forget to leave a tip?

00:20:31.295 --> 00:20:32.762
It's Ezri.

00:20:32.796 --> 00:20:34.093
She... she...

00:20:34.131 --> 00:20:35.428
I can't even say it.

00:20:35.466 --> 00:20:36.831
Try.

00:20:38.469 --> 00:20:41.336
She wants to get back
together with Worf.

00:20:43.774 --> 00:20:47.005
And before the Cardassians
ever knew we were there

00:20:47.044 --> 00:20:50.343
we destroyed the entire camp
and the relay station.

00:20:51.582 --> 00:20:54.210
To General Martok...
victor of Felton Prime.

00:20:55.419 --> 00:20:56.943
Qapla'!

00:20:59.056 --> 00:21:02.583
Let me have the honor
to welcome the Dahar Master

00:21:02.626 --> 00:21:04.958
to the humble mess hall
of the Ch'Tang.

00:21:04.995 --> 00:21:05.962
Oh, sit, sit.

00:21:05.996 --> 00:21:07.793
You do me too much honor.

00:21:07.831 --> 00:21:10.959
On this voyage,
I am but the Third Officer.

00:21:11.001 --> 00:21:13.265
I expect no special treatment.

00:21:13.303 --> 00:21:15.897
May I serve you gagh,
Dahar Master?

00:21:15.939 --> 00:21:18.806
Have you settled on
an attack plan

00:21:18.842 --> 00:21:20.469
for the starbase on Trelka V?

00:21:23.147 --> 00:21:25.479
I'm going to send
the Malpara and the Ning'tao

00:21:25.516 --> 00:21:26.949
in ahead of the rest
of the squadron.

00:21:26.984 --> 00:21:27.951
They'll make

00:21:27.985 --> 00:21:29.612
a single strafing run
of the base

00:21:29.653 --> 00:21:31.518
then head out of the system.

00:21:31.555 --> 00:21:33.455
When the enemy sends out
their repair crews

00:21:33.490 --> 00:21:36.584
to assess the damage,
then the rest

00:21:36.627 --> 00:21:38.652
of the squadron will de-cloak.

00:21:38.695 --> 00:21:41.493
With any luck, we'll catch
them not only unprepared

00:21:41.532 --> 00:21:44.899
but with their entire damage
control effort under way.

00:21:44.935 --> 00:21:45.959
Excellent.

00:21:46.003 --> 00:21:48.471
An excellent plan, General.

00:21:48.505 --> 00:21:50.166
I'm glad you approve.

00:21:50.207 --> 00:21:51.174
Of course.

00:21:51.208 --> 00:21:53.005
It's the same tactic
Kang and I used

00:21:53.110 --> 00:21:55.806
against the Federation
in the Battle of Caleb IV.

00:21:55.846 --> 00:21:57.370
You were at Caleb IV?

00:21:57.414 --> 00:21:59.109
Of course he was.

00:21:59.149 --> 00:22:00.946
Forgive the ignorance
of these children.

00:22:02.152 --> 00:22:03.949
I was a young officer once.

00:22:03.987 --> 00:22:06.683
I know how irrelevant
the past can seem.

00:22:06.723 --> 00:22:07.690
We would be honored

00:22:07.724 --> 00:22:09.123
if you would tell us
about Caleb IV.

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:11.127
Tell the tale.

00:22:11.161 --> 00:22:12.185
Tell us.

00:22:12.229 --> 00:22:14.595
Well, there's not much
to tell, really.

00:22:14.631 --> 00:22:15.962
The battle was over

00:22:16.066 --> 00:22:18.967
almost before the Federation
knew it had begun.

00:22:19.036 --> 00:22:22.631
I commanded the First Division
from the Klothos...

00:22:22.673 --> 00:22:25.164
one of the old D-5 cruisers.

00:22:25.209 --> 00:22:27.439
Kang commanded
the Second Division.

00:22:27.478 --> 00:22:30.970
Now, you must remember
that in those days

00:22:31.048 --> 00:22:35.144
the cloaking device was
a new piece of technology.

00:22:36.186 --> 00:22:38.120
There were only
a handful of engineers

00:22:38.155 --> 00:22:40.851
in the lmperial Fleet
who knew how to operate them.

00:22:40.891 --> 00:22:42.859
Before we left Chronos

00:22:42.893 --> 00:22:44.986
I spent three days
in the Engine Room

00:22:45.095 --> 00:22:48.064
taking the device apart
with my bare hands...

00:22:49.566 --> 00:22:51.500
and then putting it
back together again.

00:22:51.535 --> 00:22:52.968
Now, this would come in handy

00:22:53.003 --> 00:22:55.699
later in the battle,
as you'll see.

00:22:57.574 --> 00:22:59.303
It is not the fault
of the crew.

00:22:59.343 --> 00:23:00.810
They are not used to serving

00:23:00.844 --> 00:23:03.312
with a legendary figure
like Kor.

00:23:04.481 --> 00:23:06.381
Bridge to General Martok.

00:23:06.416 --> 00:23:08.281
Yes.

00:23:08.318 --> 00:23:09.945
We are approaching Trelka V.

00:23:10.020 --> 00:23:12.352
Set defense condition one.

00:23:13.423 --> 00:23:14.856
Defense condition one.

00:23:14.892 --> 00:23:16.792
All hands to battle stations.

00:23:16.827 --> 00:23:19.762
Repeat, all hands
to battle stations.

00:23:30.908 --> 00:23:33.308
I'm supposed to be somewhere.

00:23:33.343 --> 00:23:34.776
Dahar Master?

00:23:34.811 --> 00:23:36.472
Where are you going,
Lieutenant?

00:23:36.513 --> 00:23:37.480
To, to the Bridge.

00:23:37.514 --> 00:23:38.981
We're approaching Trelka V.

00:23:39.082 --> 00:23:40.913
The Bridge!

00:23:40.951 --> 00:23:42.145
Are you all right?

00:23:42.186 --> 00:23:43.414
Of course.

00:23:43.453 --> 00:23:45.114
What are you waiting for?

00:23:45.155 --> 00:23:46.486
Report to your station.

00:23:46.523 --> 00:23:47.512
ChaH-Veh!

00:23:49.193 --> 00:23:50.990
Concentrate!

00:24:08.312 --> 00:24:10.371
Their shields are
down to 65 percent.

00:24:10.414 --> 00:24:12.382
Three Cardassian cruisers
are in spacedock

00:24:12.416 --> 00:24:14.179
orbiting on the far
side of the planet.

00:24:14.218 --> 00:24:15.617
Two of them are
getting under way.

00:24:16.620 --> 00:24:17.780
The Malpara and the Ning'tao

00:24:17.821 --> 00:24:19.118
have completed their attack.

00:24:32.669 --> 00:24:35.229
The Malpara is gone...

00:24:36.406 --> 00:24:38.271
No survivors.

00:24:38.308 --> 00:24:40.469
The Ning'tao is heading
out of the system.

00:24:40.510 --> 00:24:41.909
The Cardassians are pursuing.

00:24:41.945 --> 00:24:44.846
And leaving their base
unprotected.

00:24:44.881 --> 00:24:46.109
Helm, take us in.

00:24:46.149 --> 00:24:48.982
Bring us to a hover
300 meters above the base.

00:24:49.019 --> 00:24:52.216
Stand by to de-cloak
on my command.

00:24:52.256 --> 00:24:54.383
Holding at 300 meters.

00:24:54.424 --> 00:24:55.618
Scan the base.

00:24:55.659 --> 00:24:57.684
They've dispatched
damage control teams.

00:24:57.728 --> 00:24:59.525
Two defense batteries are out.

00:25:00.631 --> 00:25:02.929
And they've just dropped
their primary shield grid.

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:04.934
De-cloak the ship

00:25:04.968 --> 00:25:06.663
and open fire.

00:25:21.852 --> 00:25:24.150
Shields are down to 85 percent.

00:25:25.289 --> 00:25:27.951
Reroute emergency power
to secondary shield emitters.

00:25:28.025 --> 00:25:30.152
Fire torpedoes!

00:25:31.862 --> 00:25:34.057
Helm, lay in an escape course.

00:25:35.132 --> 00:25:36.759
Aye, sir.

00:25:47.644 --> 00:25:48.736
Continue firing.

00:25:48.779 --> 00:25:50.679
Target their primary reactors.

00:25:50.714 --> 00:25:51.772
ChaH-Veh.

00:25:51.815 --> 00:25:53.544
And bring us around
for another pass.

00:25:53.583 --> 00:25:54.481
Coming about.

00:25:54.518 --> 00:25:57.009
No... only one pass.

00:26:04.795 --> 00:26:06.729
Leave the system.

00:26:08.765 --> 00:26:10.824
Do not worry, my friend.

00:26:10.867 --> 00:26:11.891
All is well.

00:26:11.935 --> 00:26:14.233
You old... fool!

00:26:14.271 --> 00:26:16.205
The Orantho reports

00:26:16.239 --> 00:26:17.934
their Captain
and First Officer are dead.

00:26:18.008 --> 00:26:19.600
They have a hull breach
in their port quarter.

00:26:19.643 --> 00:26:21.736
Instruct them to continue firing

00:26:21.778 --> 00:26:23.973
and open a channel to Kang.

00:26:24.981 --> 00:26:25.948
To Kang?

00:26:25.982 --> 00:26:27.779
Tell him we've succeeded

00:26:27.818 --> 00:26:30.753
and that the Federation
outpost on Caleb IV

00:26:30.787 --> 00:26:33.119
will be taken within an hour.

00:26:35.125 --> 00:26:37.184
Sir, Kang has been dead
for years.

00:26:39.396 --> 00:26:40.863
Prepare a boarding party.

00:26:40.897 --> 00:26:42.660
We're going to take the base.

00:26:42.699 --> 00:26:44.792
But, sir, they have
a garrison of 10,000.

00:26:44.835 --> 00:26:48.498
By the hand of Kahless,
get us out of here!

00:26:49.940 --> 00:26:51.407
Victory is ours.

00:26:51.441 --> 00:26:53.807
The Federation
will rue the day

00:26:53.844 --> 00:26:57.644
they dared to challenge
the might of the Klingon Empire.

00:26:57.681 --> 00:27:00.275
We will take Caleb IV

00:27:00.317 --> 00:27:04.519
and raise our banner
over the smoking ruins

00:27:04.652 --> 00:27:05.619
of their outpost.

00:27:11.459 --> 00:27:13.791
Escape course, now!

00:27:20.468 --> 00:27:22.834
Engage cloaks.

00:27:27.275 --> 00:27:29.743
Orantho and Slivin
have cloaked.

00:27:29.777 --> 00:27:31.938
No pursuit from Trelka V.

00:27:32.046 --> 00:27:34.105
No time to waste.

00:27:34.148 --> 00:27:37.208
Proceed... proceed
to the rendezvous

00:27:37.251 --> 00:27:38.775
and then on
to the Manora shipyards.

00:27:38.819 --> 00:27:40.480
Warp 7.

00:27:40.521 --> 00:27:41.886
Medical team to the Bridge.

00:27:41.923 --> 00:27:46.383
Worf, get that man out of here.

00:28:26.100 --> 00:28:28.364
Hi. I think
I'm in the mood for a...

00:28:28.402 --> 00:28:29.630
Wait.

00:28:29.670 --> 00:28:31.433
I have something to say.

00:28:32.573 --> 00:28:36.441
Now, you may think
this is none of my business

00:28:36.477 --> 00:28:37.944
but someone has to speak up

00:28:38.012 --> 00:28:40.037
and I've decided
that someone is me.

00:28:40.081 --> 00:28:42.572
So, here it is.
I'll just say it.

00:28:42.617 --> 00:28:44.312
Okay.

00:28:52.326 --> 00:28:53.725
You're making a mistake

00:28:53.761 --> 00:28:56.355
by pursuing another
relationship with Worf.

00:28:56.397 --> 00:28:57.921
Excuse me?

00:28:57.965 --> 00:28:58.932
You heard me.

00:28:58.966 --> 00:29:01.161
I know how Jadzia
felt about Worf

00:29:01.202 --> 00:29:03.329
but that was her life,
not yours.

00:29:03.371 --> 00:29:05.100
You're Ezri Dax.

00:29:05.139 --> 00:29:06.538
You need to give yourself

00:29:06.574 --> 00:29:09.407
a chance to explore
other relationships.

00:29:09.443 --> 00:29:12.571
You're young... and beautiful

00:29:12.613 --> 00:29:14.547
and full of life.

00:29:14.582 --> 00:29:17.881
Why go after a man
who's only a memory to you?

00:29:17.918 --> 00:29:20.284
I've had my problems
with Worf, I'll admit that

00:29:20.321 --> 00:29:21.913
but this is not about
me or my feelings.

00:29:21.989 --> 00:29:23.820
This is about you.

00:29:23.858 --> 00:29:28.693
Worf has done nothing,
and I mean nothing

00:29:28.729 --> 00:29:30.026
to deserve you.

00:29:32.166 --> 00:29:33.497
Shouldn't you try
and find someone

00:29:33.534 --> 00:29:38.164
who's willing to win your heart
not just inherit it?

00:29:38.205 --> 00:29:40.696
You deserve better.

00:29:40.741 --> 00:29:42.902
There.
I've said my piece.

00:29:46.080 --> 00:29:48.310
Can I say something now?

00:29:50.151 --> 00:29:53.780
I'm not interested in having
another relationship with Worf.

00:29:53.821 --> 00:29:55.482
I care about him

00:29:55.523 --> 00:29:58.617
and I probably always will,
but he's moved on with his life

00:29:58.659 --> 00:29:59.785
and so have I.

00:29:59.827 --> 00:30:01.692
Oh. Well, good.

00:30:02.730 --> 00:30:05.699
And I'd also like to say
that what you just did

00:30:05.733 --> 00:30:08.827
was one of the kindest,
dearest, and for you

00:30:08.869 --> 00:30:10.962
one of the most
embarrassing things

00:30:11.005 --> 00:30:12.097
that I have ever heard.

00:30:18.279 --> 00:30:20.076
You're a real sweetheart.

00:30:23.150 --> 00:30:24.617
Can I order now?

00:30:24.652 --> 00:30:25.812
Mm-hmm.

00:30:25.853 --> 00:30:27.684
A Moscow mule.

00:30:27.722 --> 00:30:29.155
Coming right up.

00:30:37.098 --> 00:30:38.395
Did you hear that?

00:30:38.432 --> 00:30:40.457
She called me "sweetheart."

00:30:40.501 --> 00:30:41.798
Yeah? So?

00:30:41.836 --> 00:30:43.861
She loves me.

00:30:43.904 --> 00:30:45.701
What?

00:30:46.741 --> 00:30:47.969
"Sweetheart."

00:30:49.176 --> 00:30:52.009
You're certifiable,
you do realize that?

00:30:52.113 --> 00:30:53.910
She loves me.

00:30:56.684 --> 00:30:58.447
Find out what's wrong
with the Ning'tao.

00:30:58.486 --> 00:31:00.317
I know Captain Lurkan is young

00:31:00.354 --> 00:31:02.447
but he must realize
the importance...

00:31:06.627 --> 00:31:08.720
the importance
of keeping formation.

00:31:11.098 --> 00:31:14.090
I've been thinking
about our next objective.

00:31:14.135 --> 00:31:16.365
Perhaps we should
go after a bigger target

00:31:16.403 --> 00:31:18.337
something more threatening
to our forces.

00:31:18.372 --> 00:31:22.035
Now, what about the base
on Caleb IV?

00:31:23.144 --> 00:31:26.204
If you'll excuse me,
I have duties to attend to.

00:31:26.247 --> 00:31:28.579
Your duties are right here.

00:31:33.888 --> 00:31:35.651
Someone was just telling me

00:31:35.689 --> 00:31:37.714
about the defenses
on Caleb IV.

00:31:37.758 --> 00:31:38.986
Who was that?

00:31:39.093 --> 00:31:42.426
I believe it was
our Third Officer, General.

00:31:42.463 --> 00:31:45.432
That's right.
Third Officer.

00:31:45.466 --> 00:31:47.525
Tell us about Caleb IV.

00:31:47.568 --> 00:31:50.765
Is it manned by Jem'Hadar
or Cardassian troops?

00:31:50.805 --> 00:31:52.466
I thought it was
a Federation outpost.

00:31:52.506 --> 00:31:54.474
How can that be?

00:31:54.508 --> 00:31:56.373
The Federation is our ally.

00:31:56.410 --> 00:31:58.776
Surely Kor is aware of that.

00:31:58.813 --> 00:32:00.940
Perhaps he's confused.

00:32:00.981 --> 00:32:03.950
Confused? The Dahar Master?

00:32:04.018 --> 00:32:05.144
Surely not.

00:32:05.186 --> 00:32:07.620
We must be the ones
who are confused.

00:32:07.655 --> 00:32:09.282
Enlighten us.

00:32:09.323 --> 00:32:11.621
Who mans the base on Caleb IV...

00:32:11.659 --> 00:32:14.287
Dominion or Federation?

00:32:15.529 --> 00:32:17.429
I think he's forgotten.

00:32:17.464 --> 00:32:18.954
I think he's asleep.

00:32:19.066 --> 00:32:20.226
Stop it!

00:32:20.267 --> 00:32:21.359
Both of you.

00:32:22.736 --> 00:32:25.466
Don't you have any respect

00:32:25.506 --> 00:32:28.839
for one of the greatest
heroes of the Empire?

00:32:29.844 --> 00:32:31.709
He's thinking it over.

00:32:31.745 --> 00:32:33.872
Give him time.

00:32:35.683 --> 00:32:41.622
The last son of the House
of Kor should not be rushed.

00:32:41.655 --> 00:32:44.783
How long should we wait?

00:32:44.825 --> 00:32:46.759
Perhaps we should ask Kang!

00:32:56.370 --> 00:32:58.531
Well, say something, old man

00:32:58.572 --> 00:33:02.338
or have you lost your tongue
as well as your mind?

00:33:08.949 --> 00:33:13.545
Savor the fruit of life,
my young friends.

00:33:13.587 --> 00:33:18.115
It has a sweet taste
when it is fresh from the vine

00:33:18.158 --> 00:33:21.127
but don't live too long.

00:33:21.161 --> 00:33:24.562
The taste turns bitter...

00:33:25.833 --> 00:33:28.825
after a time.

00:33:45.753 --> 00:33:47.414
The new personnel roster.

00:33:52.793 --> 00:33:55.284
You've removed Kor
from active duty.

00:33:55.329 --> 00:33:57.354
I saw no other choice.

00:33:57.398 --> 00:33:58.695
Still, you're his friend.

00:33:58.732 --> 00:34:00.632
It must have been
difficult for you.

00:34:00.668 --> 00:34:02.295
A friend would not have put him

00:34:02.336 --> 00:34:04.327
in that position
in the first place.

00:34:07.107 --> 00:34:10.804
I've hated his name
for almost 30 years.

00:34:10.844 --> 00:34:14.245
I've dreamt of the moment
when I would finally see him

00:34:14.281 --> 00:34:16.044
stripped of his rank and title

00:34:16.083 --> 00:34:17.880
when he would
suddenly find himself

00:34:17.918 --> 00:34:19.442
without a friend in the world

00:34:19.486 --> 00:34:22.182
without the power
of his birthright.

00:34:23.991 --> 00:34:26.653
Well, I've had that moment now.

00:34:29.430 --> 00:34:31.796
And I took no joy from it.

00:34:34.435 --> 00:34:35.959
Have you thought about
what will become of him

00:34:36.003 --> 00:34:38.938
when we return to Deep Space 9?

00:34:38.973 --> 00:34:41.100
I plan to speak
with Chancellor Gowron

00:34:41.141 --> 00:34:46.443
to try and find Kor some
assignment on the Homeworld.

00:34:47.614 --> 00:34:50.242
I'll have a word
with Gowron as well.

00:34:50.284 --> 00:34:52.582
Bridge to General Martok.

00:34:52.619 --> 00:34:53.813
Yes?

00:34:53.854 --> 00:34:55.412
Pardon the interruption, sir.

00:34:55.456 --> 00:34:58.983
Our sensors have detected
a large body of enemy ships.

00:34:59.093 --> 00:35:00.424
On my way.

00:35:03.097 --> 00:35:04.428
Where are they?

00:35:04.465 --> 00:35:06.763
Their warp signatures
are bearing directly astern.

00:35:06.800 --> 00:35:08.461
They're Jem'Hadar fighters

00:35:08.502 --> 00:35:10.299
and they appear
to be pursuing us.

00:35:10.337 --> 00:35:11.804
How can that be?

00:35:11.839 --> 00:35:14.706
The lead ship is using some sort
of long-range tachyon scanner

00:35:14.742 --> 00:35:15.936
to penetrate our cloaks.

00:35:15.976 --> 00:35:18.103
Does the Dominion possess
such a device?

00:35:18.145 --> 00:35:19.407
They do now.

00:35:19.446 --> 00:35:20.674
How many ships?

00:35:20.714 --> 00:35:22.579
I've identified
ten vessels so far.

00:35:23.917 --> 00:35:26.078
And they're gaining on us.

00:35:34.194 --> 00:35:36.958
How long before we are
within their weapons' range?

00:35:37.064 --> 00:35:38.895
Two hours, 12 minutes.

00:35:38.932 --> 00:35:41.901
Helm... have you located
the Defiant?

00:35:41.935 --> 00:35:43.562
Yes, sir.
They're waiting for us

00:35:43.604 --> 00:35:46.630
in the Kalandra Sector with
seven Federation starships.

00:35:46.673 --> 00:35:47.765
It will take us...

00:35:47.808 --> 00:35:50.538
three hours, 45 minutes
to reach them.

00:35:51.545 --> 00:35:52.807
If the Jem'Hadar could be forced

00:35:52.846 --> 00:35:55.280
to drop out of warp
for only ten minutes

00:35:55.315 --> 00:35:57.306
they would not have time
to catch up with us

00:35:57.351 --> 00:35:59.114
before we rendezvous
with the Defiant.

00:35:59.153 --> 00:36:02.122
It's a fine theory,
but how do we execute it?

00:36:03.323 --> 00:36:04.790
We could disrupt
their warp fields

00:36:04.825 --> 00:36:07.259
with an inverse graviton burst.

00:36:07.294 --> 00:36:09.125
It would force them
to drop to impulse

00:36:09.163 --> 00:36:10.926
until the gravitons dissipated.

00:36:11.031 --> 00:36:12.623
We would need to generate
a massive burst

00:36:12.666 --> 00:36:14.759
to disrupt the warp fields
of a fleet that size.

00:36:14.802 --> 00:36:17.134
A single bird-of-prey
could do it by diverting

00:36:17.171 --> 00:36:18.763
warp power
to the main deflector.

00:36:18.806 --> 00:36:19.932
How long would that delay them?

00:36:19.973 --> 00:36:22.237
They could
reinitialize their warp cores

00:36:22.276 --> 00:36:23.368
in less than two minutes.

00:36:24.611 --> 00:36:28.274
If I could engage them in battle
while they are still at impulse

00:36:28.315 --> 00:36:30.681
that would delay
them even longer.

00:36:30.717 --> 00:36:32.651
I know I could do it.

00:36:32.686 --> 00:36:34.813
What do you mean,
you could do it?

00:36:34.855 --> 00:36:37.380
The Orantho's Captain
and First Officer are dead

00:36:37.424 --> 00:36:39.654
and the Slivin's
deflector is damaged

00:36:39.693 --> 00:36:42.059
and cannot generate
a graviton burst...

00:36:42.096 --> 00:36:45.725
and the Ning'tao's Captain
is too young and inexperienced.

00:36:46.800 --> 00:36:48.734
I am the logical choice.

00:36:50.404 --> 00:36:52.702
But Worf...

00:36:52.739 --> 00:36:55.071
this means that
you'd be sacrificing

00:36:55.109 --> 00:36:59.307
the... entire crew
of the Ning'tao.

00:36:59.346 --> 00:37:01.906
I have thought about that.

00:37:01.949 --> 00:37:04.110
We could beam
most of the crew over

00:37:04.151 --> 00:37:05.584
before I take command.

00:37:05.619 --> 00:37:08.747
I would only need
six volunteers.

00:37:18.265 --> 00:37:20.699
Signal the Ning'tao.

00:37:20.734 --> 00:37:23.760
Tell them to prepare
for a change in command.

00:37:28.974 --> 00:37:30.441
Yes?

00:37:32.778 --> 00:37:34.575
I'm not hungry.

00:37:34.613 --> 00:37:36.638
The food is for me.

00:37:36.682 --> 00:37:39.344
I haven't eaten in hours.

00:37:39.385 --> 00:37:41.080
Men of our generation

00:37:41.120 --> 00:37:43.418
never stood on ceremony, huh?

00:37:44.556 --> 00:37:46.421
We ate when we were hungry.

00:37:46.458 --> 00:37:48.722
We fought when we were angered.

00:37:48.761 --> 00:37:54.597
Oh... I miss the simplicity
of those days.

00:37:54.633 --> 00:37:57.466
I miss a great deal
about those days.

00:37:57.503 --> 00:37:59.937
The warriors on this ship...

00:37:59.972 --> 00:38:02.634
they don't know
what they've missed

00:38:02.675 --> 00:38:05.269
but such is the way
with children.

00:38:05.310 --> 00:38:06.538
Hmm?

00:38:06.578 --> 00:38:09.240
They often let the
promise of the future

00:38:09.281 --> 00:38:12.114
obscure the glories
of the past.

00:38:12.151 --> 00:38:15.518
Is there a point
to this nostalgic indulgence?

00:38:15.554 --> 00:38:19.046
Only that they are children.

00:38:19.091 --> 00:38:23.926
Even Martok, who, for all
his flaws, is a great man

00:38:23.962 --> 00:38:29.298
even Martok is but a child
compared to you or me.

00:38:29.334 --> 00:38:33.293
They are quick to judge,
but slow to forgive.

00:38:33.338 --> 00:38:36.398
They still have much to learn.

00:38:39.778 --> 00:38:43.714
We are being pursued
by a Jem'Hadar fleet.

00:38:45.150 --> 00:38:49.746
Worf believes he can stop them
with a single ship.

00:38:49.788 --> 00:38:50.982
How?

00:38:53.492 --> 00:38:55.289
It's a good plan...

00:38:55.327 --> 00:38:58.057
but it has one flaw.

00:38:58.097 --> 00:39:00.930
It depends entirely
on Worf successfully

00:39:00.966 --> 00:39:03.696
engaging the whole enemy fleet

00:39:03.736 --> 00:39:06.796
if only for a short time.

00:39:09.575 --> 00:39:11.304
It can be done.

00:39:11.343 --> 00:39:13.743
The key is to confuse
their sensors

00:39:13.779 --> 00:39:18.409
in the opening moments...
with a spread of torpedoes.

00:39:18.450 --> 00:39:19.678
Perhaps.

00:39:21.086 --> 00:39:24.852
But it would take a man
with three times his experience

00:39:24.890 --> 00:39:27.120
to accomplish such a feat

00:39:27.159 --> 00:39:33.496
and such a man... would have
to be certain of his abilities.

00:39:33.532 --> 00:39:37.024
Such a man
would not take the job...

00:39:38.637 --> 00:39:41.367
unless he were certain.

00:39:47.012 --> 00:39:52.075
It has been an honor serving
with you, Kor, son of Rynar.

00:40:07.366 --> 00:40:08.697
Worf!

00:40:11.804 --> 00:40:15.103
Leaving for the Ning'tao,
I take it?

00:40:15.140 --> 00:40:16.266
Yes.

00:40:16.308 --> 00:40:17.969
I wanted to wish you well.

00:40:18.076 --> 00:40:22.376
I look forward to seeing you
at the gates to Sto-Vo-Kor.

00:40:23.882 --> 00:40:25.782
As do I.

00:40:25.818 --> 00:40:27.251
Do you have any message

00:40:27.286 --> 00:40:29.846
you want me to convey
to Jadzia?

00:40:34.693 --> 00:40:37.287
When I reach the Halls
of the Hallowed Dead

00:40:37.329 --> 00:40:39.422
I will find your beloved

00:40:39.464 --> 00:40:42.991
and remind her that her husband
is a noble warrior

00:40:43.101 --> 00:40:47.094
and that he still loves
no one but her.

00:40:47.139 --> 00:40:50.165
Good-bye, my friend.

00:40:50.209 --> 00:40:51.801
Live well.

00:41:02.688 --> 00:41:04.679
Long live the Empire.

00:41:26.044 --> 00:41:27.739
On the Bridge?

00:41:27.779 --> 00:41:31.112
If they succeed, you can
drink to their courage...

00:41:31.149 --> 00:41:32.616
and if they fail

00:41:32.651 --> 00:41:35.142
you can still drink
to their courage.

00:41:35.187 --> 00:41:37.621
The Ning'tao
is closing on the enemy.

00:41:37.656 --> 00:41:40.284
She's initiated
the graviton burst.

00:41:40.325 --> 00:41:43.453
Their warp fields
are destabilizing.

00:41:43.495 --> 00:41:45.690
They're dropping to impulse.

00:41:45.731 --> 00:41:47.164
By Kahless' hand... how many?

00:41:48.200 --> 00:41:49.633
All of them.

00:41:49.668 --> 00:41:51.863
The Ning'tao has
dropped out of warp.

00:41:51.904 --> 00:41:53.428
She's engaging the enemy.

00:41:56.341 --> 00:41:58.332
Die well, Worf.

00:41:59.878 --> 00:42:02.438
Today was not my day to die.

00:42:04.182 --> 00:42:05.706
Worf!

00:42:05.751 --> 00:42:08.219
But then who...?

00:42:08.253 --> 00:42:09.845
Kor!

00:42:09.888 --> 00:42:12.379
He surprised me
outside the transporter room

00:42:12.424 --> 00:42:13.550
with a hypospray.

00:42:15.560 --> 00:42:18.961
I hope that old fool
understands what he's doing.

00:42:19.064 --> 00:42:20.531
How goes the battle?

00:42:20.565 --> 00:42:23.329
We're approaching the limit
of our sensor range...

00:42:23.368 --> 00:42:26.394
but it appears that the enemy
formation has collapsed.

00:42:26.438 --> 00:42:28.668
The Ning'tao is
maneuvering rapidly.

00:42:28.707 --> 00:42:32.234
She's taking heavy fire
from the Jem'Hadar.

00:42:35.247 --> 00:42:37.238
I've lost contact.

00:42:37.282 --> 00:42:42.151
One ship... against ten...

00:42:42.187 --> 00:42:44.382
it doesn't seem possible.

00:42:44.423 --> 00:42:45.890
He will succeed.

00:42:45.924 --> 00:42:48.085
He is Kor...

00:42:48.126 --> 00:42:50.356
the Dahar Master.

00:43:01.139 --> 00:43:02.606
He's done it.

00:43:02.641 --> 00:43:04.632
The Jem'Hadar are out of time.

00:43:04.676 --> 00:43:08.840
They can no longer overtake us
before we reach the Defiant.

00:43:08.880 --> 00:43:12.338
How... how did
that pompous old man

00:43:12.384 --> 00:43:14.750
hold off an entire
Jem'Hadar fleet

00:43:14.786 --> 00:43:16.777
with only one ship?

00:43:16.822 --> 00:43:18.756
Does it matter?

00:43:21.593 --> 00:43:24.323
Darok, give me that bottle.

00:43:27.299 --> 00:43:29.267
To Kor...

00:43:29.301 --> 00:43:31.166
the Dahar Master...

00:43:31.203 --> 00:43:33.694
a noble warrior to the end.

00:43:36.408 --> 00:43:42.643
My-cho Qara, end-do keela

00:43:42.681 --> 00:43:48.244
bay-doH chum,
ka ree-do meela

00:43:48.286 --> 00:43:51.517
Stum-pa rip-to

00:43:51.556 --> 00:43:55.549
Maah-la ee'qo

00:43:55.594 --> 00:43:58.392
ree-kaH!

00:43:58.430 --> 00:44:04.665
Ree-kaH! Ree-kaH!

00:44:04.703 --> 00:44:07.934
Maah, so faH ka'lee

00:44:08.040 --> 00:44:11.008
te cho-paH...
